B. Exact title-to-file association

This is a mandatory integrity requirement.

When an administrator enters a title and uploads a document:

- Save the exact title in the database.
- Save the uploaded document in persistent storage.
- Generate a unique file-storage key.
- Store that key in the corresponding proposal record.
- Associate the proposal with that exact document using a stable identifier.
- Preserve the original filename separately from the public proposal title.

The public page must display the exact saved title and retrieve the file associated with that specific database record.

Never:

- Derive the public title from the filename when a custom title exists.
- Match files only by filename.
- Assume file order corresponds to database record order.
- Substitute one proposal's document for another.
- Use mock data or generated documents when a real file is missing.
- Silently return a different file when a request fails.

